      "writtenOn": "2021-09-03T11:19:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "With this, the code *requires* that SYSTEM \u003e NETWORK \u003e NONE.\n\nWhat I dislike is that this is not explicit anywhere in the file. One thing you could do is :\n- Have a test that ensures that SYSTEM \u003e NETWORK and NETWORK \u003e NONE\n- Add a comment here saying a strict order of permissions is required, and it is enforced in tests\n\nAlternatively, you could test in the constructor and throw if it\u0027s not true, but it\u0027s uncustomary to have this kind of thing in production code.\n\nIf you choose to keep the constants in this file, having a comment about strict ordering above them is also good.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 261,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 261,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "f0edb23bce5674bd1360741a4f43c40eeae6c69b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dd67eb66_708828b5",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/connectivity/PermissionMonitor.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 373,
