      "writtenOn": "2021-09-03T11:19:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Now that we have ints I realize this is fairly dangerous ; what if we mistakenly store NONE in mApps anywhere ? Then this would assign the network permission to this app.\n\nSuggest skipping the UID explicitly if the permission is NONE. E.g. :\n\n  for (int \u003d 0, i \u003c apps.size(); i++) {\n    final int permission \u003d apps.valueAt(i);\n    if (NONE \u003d\u003d permission) continue; // Normally NONE is not stored in this map, but just in case\n    final List\u003cInteger\u003e list \u003d (SYSTEM \u003d\u003d permission) ? system : network;\n\nAlternatively, you could have a List\u003cInteger\u003e[] indexed by permission, and make the code more generic. But maybe it\u0027s not worth it at this point.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 373,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 373,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "f0edb23bce5674bd1360741a4f43c40eeae6c69b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
